    {
      "text": "Stick, here’s a concrete, repeatable workflow you can run locally (or in CI) to:\n\n1. **Diff the current outputs against a reference**  \n2. **Prune any “bad” artifacts**  \n3. **Commit the cleanup and push**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pull the latest state\n\n```bash\ngit fetch origin\ngit checkout main          # or the branch you work on\ngit reset --hard origin/main\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Generate / collect the new outputs  \n\nAssuming your build step writes files to `output/`:\n\n```bash\n# Example build command – replace with yours\n./build.sh   # or `make`, `npm run build`, etc.\n```\n\nMake sure the new output directory is populated (e.g., `output/`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Compare against the previous good baseline  \n\nIf you keep the last “good” results in a Git‑tracked directory `baseline/`:\n\n```bash\n# Show a concise diff of file contents\ngit diff --no-index baseline/ output/ > diff_summary.txt\n```\n\n- **Zero‑diff** ⇒ everything matches.  \n- **Non‑zero diff** ⇒ inspect `diff_summary.txt`. Lines prefixed with `+` are new/changed; `-` are missing/removed.\n\nYou can also use `diff -qr` for a quick “are they identical?” check:\n\n```bash\ndiff -qr baseline/ output/\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Identify “bad artifacts”\n\nDefine what constitutes a bad artifact—common patterns include:\n\n| Pattern | Typical cause | Example filter |\n|---------|---------------|----------------|\n| Files > 5 MiB (unused binaries) | Stale build artifacts | `find output/ -type f -size +5M` |\n| Zero‑byte files | Failed generation step | `find output/ -type f -size 0` |\n| Temporary suffixes (`*.tmp`, `*_old`) | Leftover temp files | `find output/ -type f \\( -name \"*.tmp\" -o -name \"*_old*\" \\)` |\n| Known bad hashes (checksum list) | Corrupted data | `md5sum -c bad_hashes.txt` |\n\nPut the filters you need into a small script:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# 1️⃣ Remove oversized files\nfind output/ -type f -size +5M -print -delete\n\n# 2️⃣ Remove empty files\nfind output/ -type f -size 0 -print -delete\n\n# 3️⃣ Remove temp/old files\nfind output/ -type f \\( -name \"*.tmp\" -o -name \"*_old*\" \\) -print -delete\n```\n\nSave it as `clean_artifacts.sh` and run:\n\n```bash\nchmod +x clean_artifacts.sh\n./clean_artifacts.sh\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verify the cleanup\n\nRe‑run the diff to ensure only intended changes remain:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --no-index baseline/ output/ > post_cleanup_diff.txt\n# Quick sanity check\ndiff -qr baseline/ output/\n```\n\nIf `post_cleanup_diff.txt` still shows unexpected differences, iterate on the filters until the diff matches expectations.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Commit the cleaned output\n\nIf the `output/` directory is tracked (or you’re storing it in a separate branch):\n\n```bash\ngit add output/\ngit status                # sanity check what’s staged\ngit commit -m \"Cleanup: remove bad artifacts after output generation\"\n```\n\n*Optional:* Tag the commit for traceability:\n\n```bash\ngit tag -a \"cleanup-$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)\" -m \"Automated cleanup\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Push the changes\n\n```bash\ngit push origin main        # or the appropriate branch\n# If you created a tag\ngit push origin --tags\n```\n\n---\n\n### One‑liner for CI pipelines\n\nIf you want this baked into a CI job (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, etc.):\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/cleanup.yml\nname: Cleanup Outputs\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  cleanup:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - name: Build\n        run: ./build.sh\n      - name: Clean artifacts\n        run: |\n          find output/ -type f -size +5M -delete\n          find output/ -type f -size 0 -delete\n          find output/ -type f \\( -name \"*.tmp\" -o -name \"*_old*\" \\) -delete\n      - name: Commit cleanup\n        env:\n          GIT_AUTHOR_NAME: github-actions\n          GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL: actions@github.com\n          GIT_COMMITTER_NAME: github-actions\n          GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL: actions@github.com\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"$GIT_AUTHOR_NAME\"\n          git config user.email \"$GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\"\n          git add output/\n          git commit -m \"CI: automated artifact cleanup\"\n          git push\n```\n\nReplace the `find` filters with whatever criteria you deem “bad”.\n\n---\n\n## TL;DR checklist\n\n- **Diff**: `git diff --no-index baseline/ output/` → spot changes.  \n- **Filter & delete**: `find … -delete` (size, empty, tmp, etc.).  \n- **Re‑diff** to confirm only expected deltas remain.  \n- **Commit** `output/` and **push**.\n\nIf you have a specific set of files, a different directory layout, or custom “bad” definitions, let me know and I can refine the script accordingly.",
